{"key":"BugReportWindow","text":"## BugReportWindow\n\nThe **Bug Report Window** lets you file and track bugs. Each report gets a\n**BUG-####** id and is saved to shared storage on GitHub, so reports are\nvisible across accounts. You can attach screenshots to any report.\n\n---\n\n@layout\nTitle Bar | 0.50, 0.03 | Window title and standard controls.\nFilter & Sort | 0.28, 0.11 | Status filter buttons narrow the list; the Sort button reorders it.\nNew Bug | 0.85, 0.11 | \"+ New Bug\" creates a report with the next BUG-#### id.\nBug List | 0.50, 0.56 | Click a row to expand it — edit the Title, Description, and Notes, add an image with \"+ Attach Image\" (click a thumbnail to view full size), or Delete the report.\n\n---\n\n### Filtering & sorting\n\n- **Filter buttons** — show only reports matching a status\n- **Sort** — open the sort menu to reorder the list\n\n### A bug row\n\n- Click a row to expand / collapse it\n- Edit **Title**, **Description**, and **Notes** in place\n- **+ Attach Image** — add a screenshot; click a thumbnail to view it full size\n- **Delete** — remove the report (asks to confirm)\n\n### Shortcuts\n\n- **Enter** — commit the field you're typing in\n- **Esc** — cancel an in-progress entry\n\n### Status: Stable\n### Purpose: OS\n\n---","screenshot":""}